// Build settings that identify *your* build of Udha. Nothing here is secret,
// but nothing here should be another person's either.
//
// Override any of these by creating Local.xcconfig next to this file (it is
// git-ignored), e.g.
//   UDHA_BUNDLE_ID = com.yourname.udha
//   DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
// With no team set, Xcode signs to run locally, which is all a Debug build
// needs. A real team is required for the Keychain data-protection path and
// for distributing the app.

UDHA_BUNDLE_ID = ai.udha.desktop
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

// --- Entitlements: chosen by whether there is a signing team -----------------
//
// `keychain-access-groups` requires a provisioning profile. With no team there
// is no profile, and Xcode does not quietly drop the entitlement — it refuses
// the whole build ("has entitlements that require signing with a development
// certificate"). So a clone with no Apple account could not build at all.
//
// Two entitlement files, then, picked here rather than by hand:
//   * Udha.AIDesktop.entitlements        — the full set, needs a team
//   * Udha.AIDesktop-local.entitlements  — the same minus keychain-access-groups
//
// The selection is a composed variable name: UDHA_TEAM_TAG is the team id, or
// the literal NOTEAM when DEVELOPMENT_TEAM is empty, so UDHA_ENT_$(...) resolves
// to UDHA_ENT_NOTEAM for an unsigned build and to nothing — hence the default —
// for any real team. Setting DEVELOPMENT_TEAM in Local.xcconfig is enough;
// nothing else has to change.
//
// What an unsigned build loses: `KeychainBackend.supportsDataProtection` probes
// for the access-group keychain and falls back to the legacy per-item one, so
// macOS asks for the login password once per stored credential per launch.
UDHA_TEAM_TAG = $(DEVELOPMENT_TEAM:default=NOTEAM)
UDHA_ENT_NOTEAM = Udha.AIDesktop/Udha.AIDesktop-local.entitlements
UDHA_ENT_DEFAULT = Udha.AIDesktop/Udha.AIDesktop.entitlements
UDHA_ENTITLEMENTS = $(UDHA_ENT_$(UDHA_TEAM_TAG):default=$(UDHA_ENT_DEFAULT))

#include? "Local.xcconfig"
